# Kotlin daemon session files
.kotlin/

# The IDE's own directory, all of it.
#
# Only six paths under it were ignored before, so the other sixteen files were tracked — and
# they are not project configuration, they are a record of what one machine was doing. Which
# device you last deployed to, which devices the device manager knows about, four files of
# Copilot migration state. They change by opening the project, so every `git status` had
# something in it that nobody wrote, and switching branches failed on files the IDE had
# regenerated in the meantime.
#
# Nothing here is needed to build: Gradle is the build, and it is what CI runs. A fresh clone
# opens in Android Studio and the IDE writes these itself.
#
# JetBrains does suggest sharing `codeStyles/` and `inspectionProfiles/` across a team, and
# that is a fair argument — un-ignore those two specifically if it ever comes up. It is not
# worth the noise for the sake of one inspection profile nobody has edited.
.idea/
